1. Overview {#overview}
What is AI Control Plane?
AI Control Plane is a centralized policy and routing engine for AI services that provides:

🛡️ Data Privacy Protection - Automatically detects and redacts PII (Personal Identifiable Information)

🎯 Smart AI Routing - Routes requests to the optimal AI provider based on cost, performance, and capabilities

🔒 Security Policy Enforcement - Enforces access control and compliance policies

📊 Unified Analytics - Centralized monitoring and auditing of all AI requests

Key Features
Feature	Description
PII Detection	Automatically identifies and masks sensitive data (ID numbers, emails, phone numbers)
Multi-Provider Support	Works with OpenAI, Anthropic, Google AI, and local models (Llama, etc.)
Policy Engine	OPA-based policy enforcement for access control and compliance
Visual Dashboard	Streamlit-based UI for policy management and monitoring
REST API	Full REST API for integration with existing systems
Rate Limiting	Per-tenant rate limiting to prevent abuse
Audit Logging	Complete audit trail of all requests and decisions
Use Cases
Enterprise AI Gateway - Secure gateway for AI services in regulated industries

SaaS Multi-Tenant - Isolated AI access for multi-tenant applications

Compliance & Privacy - GDPR, POPIA, HIPAA compliance for AI usage

Cost Optimization - Smart routing to reduce AI costs

Security Layer - Additional security layer for AI services

2. Architecture {#architecture}
System Architecture
text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                     External Clients                         │
│                  (Web, Mobile, API)                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    FastAPI Application                       │
│                   (src/main.py)                              │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐     │
│  │              Middleware Layer                       │     │
│  │  • TenantMiddleware                                 │     │
│  │  • RequestIDMiddleware                              │     │
│  │  • RateLimitMiddleware                              │     │
│  │  • LoggingMiddleware                                │     │
│  │  • MetricsMiddleware                                │     │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘     │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐     │
│  │               API Routes                            │     │
│  │  • /api/v1/classify    - Text classification      │     │
│  │  • /api/v1/policy      - Policy evaluation        │     │
│  │  • /api/v1/route       - AI routing              │     │
│  │  • /api/v1/policies    - Policy management        │     │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
        ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐
        ▼                     ▼                     ▼
┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐
│   OPA        │    │  AI Providers │    │  Database    │
│   Policy     │    │  • OpenAI    │    │  PostgreSQL  │
│   Engine     │    │  • Anthropic │    │  (Optional)  │
│              │    │  • Google    │    │              │
│              │    │  • Local     │    │              │
└──────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘
Component Overview
Component	Description	Technology
API Gateway	Main entry point for all requests	FastAPI
Policy Engine	Evaluates security and compliance policies	OPA (Open Policy Agent)
Classification Engine	Detects PII and classifies content	spaCy + Custom Recognizers
AI Router	Routes requests to appropriate AI providers	Custom + Provider APIs
Dashboard	Visual management interface	Streamlit
Database	Stores policies, logs, and configurations	PostgreSQL (Optional)
Cache	Caches frequent requests for performance	Redis (Optional)
3. Installation {#installation}
Prerequisites
Python 3.10+

pip

(Optional) PostgreSQL 14+

(Optional) Redis 6+

(Optional) OPA 0.50+

Quick Start
bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/ai-control-plane.git
cd ai-control-plane

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Download spaCy model
python -m spacy download en_core_web_lg

# Set up environment variables
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your configuration

# Run the application
uvicorn src.main:app --reload
